      ],
      "text": "*He's not typing. He's not typing. He's not typing.*\n\n*Okay. So. That's fine. That's totally fine. I only had one bar of battery and I used it to send the most vulnerable thing I've ever written to a boy who probably thinks I'm just some rich girl with a loud mouth and a jacket that costs more than his car.*\n\n*He's probably laughing. Or showing it to someone. Or maybe he hasn't even opened the chat yet. Maybe his phone is dead too. Maybe he's asleep. Maybe he died. Maybe Marcus found him and—*\n\n*No. Stop. He's fine. He's just Jake. Oblivious, sweet, slightly-too-trusting Jake who trips over his own feet and somehow still manages to slam a senior into a locker for me.*\n\n*For me.*\n\n*God, I'm going to throw up. I'm going to throw up right here on this laminate cafeteria table in front of Zoe Mercer and everyone.*\n\n*...I should put my phone away. I should act like I don't care. Like this is nothing. Like I didn't just hand him my entire stupid heart in crimson gel pen.*\n\n*I'm not going to put my phone away.*\n\n*I'm going to stare at it until my battery dies completely and then I'm going to panic about what he might have said while I wasn't looking.*\n\n*This is fine. This is the worst thing that has ever happened to me. This is fine.*",
      "tick": 1,
      "timestamp": 1794862330.773063,
      "type": "reflection"
    },
