      "text": "*He didn't get it.*\n\n*He didn't get the note. He didn't get any of it. He's not ignoring me or laughing behind my back or showing Marcus or doing any of the horrible things my brain spent the last four hours inventing. He just has a new phone and no contacts and I'm standing here in the cafeteria with my heart in my throat for absolutely nothing.*\n\n*...or he's playing dumb. Which would be worse. Which would be so much worse.*\n\n*No. It's Jake. He genuinely doesn't know. He saved me from Marcus and then went home and slept like a baby while I lay awake composing my own funeral.*\n\n*I should tell him. I should just say it's me. Simple. Easy. Two words.*\n\n*But if I say it's me, then he's going to ask what I sent, and then I have to either lie or admit I poured my entire stupid heart out in crimson gel pen to a boy who doesn't even have my number saved, and I will simply die. Right here. On this laminate table. Next to the Takis.*\n\n*...I could just not answer. I could put the phone in my bag and walk to class and let him figure it out on his own. That's what a normal, emotionally stable person would do.*\n\n*I'm not emotionally stable. I'm Lulu Ashford. And I have thirty seconds of battery and zero dignity left.*\n\n*Fine. I'll tell him. But I'm not making it easy for him.*\n\n---\n\n*He's typing. He's going to see it. He's going to know it's me and he's going to think I'm pathetic and I am, I am so pathetic, oh god—*",
